	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Generate a custom YouTube RSS feed from the most recent URL in your [Clipboard History](https://www.alfredapp.com/help/features/clipboard/) or the URL in the frontmost browser tab via the `nobsyt` keyword.

![Keyword to choose a URL](images/about/keyword.png)

![Showing UI to generate filter](images/about/ui.png)

Set the filter to the types of videos you want to include in the feed and press &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; to copy it to the clipboard.</string>
